__pycache__/
*.pyc

# The action LOG is not committed - it is a record of this box, not of the code.
#
# The DIRECTORY is, and that is a deliberate divergence from
# apps/portal-files/.gitignore, which ignores `audit/` outright. Docker creates
# a missing bind source as ROOT and this container runs as uid 1000, so an
# absent directory is mounted unwritable - and audit() swallows that error by
# design, because a full disk must never block a legitimate restart. The symptom
# is therefore a silently empty audit trail rather than a failure, which is the
# worst way for an audit trail to be broken. See audit/.gitkeep.
audit/*
!audit/.gitkeep
